{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q15409361","formula":"C₂₀H₂₃NO₃","hill":"C20H23NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":20.0,"H":23.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"N-methyl-3-piperidyl benzilate"},"descriptions":{"en":"N-Methyl-3-piperidyl benzilate (JB-336 or LBJ) is an anticholinergic drug related to the chemical warfare agent 3-quinuclidinyl benzilate. N-methyl-3-piperidyl benzilate is less potent and shorter acting than 3-quinuclidyl benzilate, but like 3-QNB its effects on the central nervous system predominate over peripheral effects. It produces deliriant and hallucinogenic effects similar to those of plants such as datura and may be used recreationally at low doses; however, unpleasant side effects such as dysphoria, nausea and vomiting, dizziness and extreme dry mouth tend to make abuse of drugs of this kind uncommon."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":62495,"mass":325.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN1CCCC(C1)OC(=O)C(C2=CC=CC=C2)(C3=CC=CC=C3)O","inchikey":"ZBEILXWHVSVDBN-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"(1-methylpiperidin-3-yl) 2-hydroxy-2,2-diphenylacetate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"62495","atoms":47,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.208,"y":-0.054,"z":1.006,"el":"O"},{"x":1.258,"y":0.062,"z":2.102,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.308,"y":-1.745,"z":-0.268,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.225,"y":-1.17,"z":-0.85,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.503,"y":-0.621,"z":0.841,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.507,"y":0.232,"z":1.611,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.856,"y":-0.681,"z":-0.648,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.929,"y":-0.236,"z":1.331,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.203,"y":-0.307,"z":-0.172,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.529,"y":-1.265,"z":-2.278,"el":"C"},{"x":1.156,"y":-0.03,"z":0.677,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.178,"y":-0.721,"z":0.392,"el":"C"},{"x":1.113,"y":1.394,"z":0.111,"el":"C"},{"x":2.361,"y":-0.845,"z":0.195,"el":"C"},{"x":0.451,"y":1.609,"z":-1.074,"el":"